1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,180
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time, known for bringing his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

2
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:16,940
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon. Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store. Until one night he decided to rewrite his story.

3
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:18,560
And there was like one night.

4
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:29,640
Stay up all night long and rather than give myself excuses, I would look at everything that I'm up in my life or everything I'm not doing or whatever and just not give myself any excuses out.

5
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:35,580
Just like nail it. And I would spend like all night laying out everything I'm doing that's wrong.

6
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:38,660
And then I would spend the last two hours figuring out how I can change it.

7
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:42,480
And as opposed to just doing it and then going to get some sleep.

8
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:46,040
I decided to change my life. Today I present you the Tarantino Method.

9
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:51,000
To follow this process you'll need three things. A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night.

10
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:55,760
When the world is silent and not a soul is awake. That's when it can happen. Trust.

11
00:00:55,760 --> 00:01:24,147
Now it begins The first page is always going to be the hardest but it really all about getting that ball rolling Now that you started you have to ask yourself the big scary fear question What am I doing wrong Be brutally honest As Quinton himself would say nail it Take your time Dive deep It gritty It tough but it absolutely necessary And when you push through boom you halfway there

12
00:01:26,487 --> 00:01:37,507
It's all out there. The fears, the doubts, the mistakes, the lessons, the heartbreak, all laid out, bare for you to see. Not built up in your mind, but on paper, tangible.

13
00:01:38,927 --> 00:02:06,647
Take a moment because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it? We're not all Quentin Tarantino. You might be feeling like you're all written out. So let's make this part simple. A straightforward list. A hundred ways you can change your life. Quite a simple process. Take a mistake you've learned and write down a way to change it. Repeat it over and over again and push forward. Write it down. Adapt. Reflect. Learn and grow.

14
00:02:06,647 --> 00:02:11,827
Until finally, when you ask yourself, how can I change my life? You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

15
00:02:11,947 --> 00:02:15,367
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

16
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:17,147
You gotta actually f***ing do it.
